%% SECTION Life Cycles, Focus Areas and Processes
@@
A team prototypes a user interface three times based on user feedback before building it, and then delivers the whole product at once. Which statement best describes this life cycle?
A) Iterative development with a single delivery
B) Incremental delivery with multiple releases to users
C) Predictive with no feedback
D) Continuous delivery
= A
? Repeated refinement through prototypes is iterative; delivering everything at once is a single delivery.

@@
Which focus area contains the largest number of processes in the Eighth Edition?
A) Planning
B) Executing
C) Monitoring and Controlling
D) Initiating
= A
? Planning has 19 of the 40 processes, Monitoring and Controlling 10, Executing 8, Initiating 2 and Closing 1.

@@
Which of the following processes belongs to the Executing focus area?
A) Implement Risk Responses
B) Perform Risk Analysis
C) Monitor Risks
D) Plan Risk Responses
= A
? Implement Risk Responses is the only executing process in the Risk domain. Analysis and response planning are planning processes; Monitor Risks is monitoring and controlling.

@@
Which process belongs to the Monitoring and Controlling focus area?
A) Validate Scope
B) Develop Scope Structure
C) Define Scope
D) Elicit and Analyze Requirements
= A
? Validate Scope (formal acceptance) and Monitor and Control Scope are the two monitoring and controlling processes of the Scope domain.

@@
In which performance domain is Plan Sourcing Strategy located?
A) Governance
B) Resources
C) Finance
D) Risk
= A
? Plan Sourcing Strategy is a Governance planning process, reflecting that sourcing decisions are strategic. Acquisition and control of resources are in the Resources domain.

@@
Which Eighth Edition process replaced "Direct and Manage Project Work"?
A) Manage Project Execution
B) Lead the Team
C) Monitor and Control Project Performance
D) Manage Quality Assurance
= A
? Manage Project Execution in the Governance domain is the renamed Direct and Manage Project Work.

@@
A phase gate review concludes that the project should continue only if the scope is reduced. What decision outcome is this?
A) Continue with modifications
B) Repeat the phase
C) End the project
D) Continue without change
= A
? Phase gate decisions can be to continue, continue with modifications, repeat the phase or end the project.

@@ | multi
Which two statements about project documents and the project management plan are correct? (Choose two.)
A) The issue log can be updated without a formal change request
B) Changes to the schedule baseline require formal change control
C) The risk register is a component of the scope baseline
D) The stakeholder register is part of the cost baseline
E) Project documents can never be changed after planning
= A, B
? Project documents such as the issue log are updated as needed; baselines and the plan require change control. Registers are not baseline components.

@@
Which output is created by Initiate Project or Phase in addition to the project charter?
A) Assumption log
B) Stakeholder engagement plan
C) Risk register
D) Cost baseline
= A
? The charter and the assumption log are the key outputs of initiating the project or phase. The risk register is created in Identify Risks.

@@
A project manager compares actual progress with the plan and reports that the project is 12% behind schedule. This is an example of:
A) Work performance information
B) Work performance data
C) A deliverable
D) An enterprise environmental factor
= A
? Data that has been analysed against the plan becomes work performance information.

@@
Which development approach is usually most appropriate when the cost of change is high and requirements are stable and well understood?
A) Predictive
B) Adaptive
C) Kanban flow
D) Iterative experimentation
= A
? Predictive approaches suit stable requirements and expensive change, such as construction.

@@
Which of the following is NOT a component of the project management plan?
A) Issue log
B) Scope baseline
C) Risk management plan
D) Change management plan
= A
? The issue log is a project document. Baselines, subsidiary plans and the change management plan are plan components.

@@
In an adaptive project, when do the five focus areas occur?
A) Within each iteration, repeatedly throughout the project
B) Once each, in strict sequence, across the whole of the project
C) Only during the first iteration
D) Only during release planning
= A
? Planning, executing, monitoring and controlling, and closing occur in every iteration; initiating recurs with new releases or phases.

@@
Which two processes from the Sixth Edition were merged into Perform Risk Analysis?
A) Perform Qualitative Risk Analysis and Perform Quantitative Risk Analysis
B) Identify Risks and Perform Qualitative Risk Analysis, to speed up risk assessment
C) Plan Risk Responses and Implement Risk Responses, to link planning and action
D) Plan Risk Management and Identify Risks, to simplify early risk planning
= A
? The two analysis processes were combined into a single process covering both qualitative and quantitative techniques.

@@
A company releases a new feature to all customers at the end of every month. Which delivery cadence is this?
A) Periodic delivery
B) Continuous delivery
C) Single delivery
D) Ad hoc delivery
= A
? Fixed, regular releases are periodic. Continuous delivery releases whenever features are ready.

@@
Which process consolidates subsidiary plans into a cohesive project management plan?
A) Integrate and Align Project Plans
B) Initiate Project or Phase
C) Plan Scope Management
D) Assess and Implement Changes
= A
? Integrate and Align Project Plans is the Eighth Edition name for developing the project management plan.

@@
An organisation is unsure whether a project is clear, complicated, complex or chaotic. According to Cynefin, what is this state called?
A) Confusion (disorder)
B) Complex
C) Chaotic
D) Clear
= A
? Cynefin's central domain, confusion, applies when it is not yet known which domain the situation belongs to.

@@ | match
Match each process with its focus area.
1) Identify Stakeholders
2) Develop Budget
3) Lead the Team
4) Monitor Communications
A) Initiating
B) Planning
C) Executing
D) Monitoring and Controlling
= 1-A, 2-B, 3-C, 4-D
? Identify Stakeholders is initiating, Develop Budget planning, Lead the Team executing, and Monitor Communications monitoring and controlling.

@@
Which type of change request is a modification to a non-conforming product component?
A) Defect repair
B) Corrective action
C) Preventive action
D) Update
= A
? Defect repair modifies a non-conforming product. Corrective and preventive actions address performance; updates change controlled documents.

@@
What is the main reason for holding a kickoff meeting?
A) To align everyone on objectives, roles and the plan as the team moves into execution
B) To obtain the sponsor's signature on the project charter and formally authorise the project
C) To review lessons learned from the previous phase and close open procurements
D) To obtain formal customer acceptance of the deliverables produced so far
= A
? The kickoff aligns stakeholders and the team on objectives, roles and the plan, typically at the end of planning or the start of execution.
